<Project>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <!--
      Defect classes that must fail the build instead of scrolling past as warnings.

      These catch code that provably cannot run, which review reliably misses because the
      build still says "succeeded":

        CS0162  Unreachable code detected      (e.g. a second return after the first)
        CS0642  Possible mistaken empty statement  (e.g. `if (cond);` - the guard does nothing)
        CS0219  Variable assigned but never used

      The rest of the warning baseline (CA1416, CS0618, nullable warnings) is deliberately
      left as warnings.

      Do not add any of these three to a <NoWarn> list. NoWarn suppresses a diagnostic
      before WarningsAsErrors can promote it, so listing a code in both silently disables
      the gate for that configuration - which is how a real CS0162 in OccultCrescent.cs
      sat unreported in every Release build until this was added.
    -->
    <WarningsAsErrors>CS0162;CS0642;CS0219</WarningsAsErrors>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
